WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.337
In this video, we'll keep
my-taste current with a

2
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:10.601
weekly automation, so your
skills keep up with you.

3
00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.354
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

4
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.299
An automation is a session
that runs on a schedule.

5
00:00:18.299 --> 00:00:24.610
This one reads the week's sessions
every Monday, and updates my-taste.

6
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.440
It shows a draft first:
on this computer, Mondays at nine,

7
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.780
on Autopilot with Allow all,
and the exact prompt it will run.

8
00:00:41.297 --> 00:00:44.808
It looks right. Reply: Create it.

9
00:00:48.797 --> 00:00:51.032
It's on. The first run is Monday.

10
00:00:51.032 --> 00:00:56.519
It updates my-taste only when it finds
something new, and tells you what changed.

11
00:00:59.477 --> 00:01:02.611
You'll find it under Automations,
in the side bar.

12
00:01:06.477 --> 00:01:10.769
Open it to check the schedule,
the mode, and the permissions.

13
00:01:15.477 --> 00:01:19.318
No model was set, so it shows the default.

14
00:01:19.318 --> 00:01:23.526
Pick one, like GPT-6.2 Sol at High, then save.

15
00:01:27.977 --> 00:01:32.138
Each run costs credits, like any
session, so weekly is plenty.

16
00:01:32.138 --> 00:01:34.487
Next, we'll draft a research study.
